      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-294488",
      ":question/problem": "A quality control inspector recorded the number of defective batteries produced during $10$ different shifts. The data are displayed in the table below.\n\n| Shift | Number of defective batteries |\n| --- | ---: |\n| A | $12$ |\n| B | $15$ |\n| C | $13$ |\n| D | $11$ |\n| E | $14$ |\n| F | $15$ |\n| G | $16$ |\n| H | $13$ |\n| I | $12$ |\n| J | $14$ |\n\nWhat is the range of the number of defective batteries produced across all $10$ shifts?"
